{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/908424-is-there-any-abyssal-homebrew","id":908424,"title":"Is there any Abyssal Homebrew?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-06T10:35:13-07:00","id":908424,"title":"Is there any Abyssal Homebrew?","content":"Now, I'll outright say that I can see why the Abyssals are less likely than other splats to get &quot;until the dang books come out&quot; homebrew than anybody else: a pretty functional, if uninspiring, Abyssal can be made just by making a Solar and then covering them in black paint and skull-shaped sprinkles. However, I wanted to know if anybody had gone any farther than that and started working on charm tweaks and stuff like that, so I figured I'd ask---and if there's none yet, perhaps in my asking I might help spur somebody with ideas to write them up.<br /> <br /> What can I say? I like my Spookysolars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T11:06:09-07:00","id":908441,"title":"","content":"When the playgroup of my seafaring campaign adapted Seamstress of Dissolution, we mostly used, as you said, a Solar with black paint. For example, we tweaked Ailment-Rectifying Method so that if she somehow doesn't roll enough successes, she can make up the difference by sucking (successes she's short by) health levels' worth of blood. It's still pretty rudimentary, far from fully tested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":